==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|upholster|pos1=noun|er}},<ref>{{R:Oxford English Dictionary|volume=X|part=1|page=426|column=2|passage=f. {{smallcaps|Upholster}} ''sb.'' + {{smallcaps|-er}}<sup>1</sup> 3.|nodot=1}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|passage=earlier ''upholster'' in same sense (see uphold, -ster) + -er<sup>1</sup>}}</ref> from {{der|en|enm|upholdester}}, {{m|enm|upholster}}, from {{der|en|enm|upholder|t=dealer in small goods}}, from {{m|enm|upholden|t=to repair, uphold}}. Equivalent to {{af|en|uphold|-ster|-er}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌpˈhəʊlstəɹə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who [[upholster]]s [[furniture]], especially a trained {{l|en|craftsman}} who does so as an {{l|en|occupation}}.

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|reupholsterer}}

